  "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ 5{x}^{2} & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, the hyperbola does not intersect the line $y=x.$",
